# Linting and Type-Check Rules

- Linter errors are blocking for the code you touch. Do not introduce new lint/type failures.
- Fix newly introduced errors before continuing; do not expand scope into unrelated pre-existing issues unless asked.
- Respect ESLint/Prettier/TS configs under `Client/config/` and root TS/Vite configs.
- Use existing scripts when validating locally (full gate list: [`ci-gates.mdc`](ci-gates.mdc)):
  - From `Client/`: `pnpm lint`, `pnpm format`, `pnpm typecheck` as needed (see `Client/package.json`).
  - Repo-wide: `./scripts/run-all-linters.sh [client|server|all]`.
- Do not disable rules without justification; prefer code changes over suppression.
- **UI Component Standardization**: Ensure all buttons and text use standardized components from **`Client/packages/ui/`**. See [`ui-components.mdc`](../frontend/ui-components.mdc) for detailed rules.
